from pathlib import Path
import json
p=Path('outputs/wendys_segment_facets/Wendys_Segment_Facets.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())
texts=[
'Wendy’s sells hamburger-led quick-service meals, including chicken sandwiches and nuggets, chili, fries, baked potatoes, salads, beverages, Frosty desserts and children’s meals. The Q2 2026 MD&A also identifies breakfast in the U.S. and Canada. This describes food products, rather than franchise support or property-leasing services; menu availability should not be assumed identical across international markets.',
'The company operates restaurants, franchises the Wendy’s brand and operating system, and provides restaurant-property leasing, subleasing and development support. Consumers purchase meals, while franchisees receive business support and may lease restaurant premises. These customer relationships generate different revenues and should be evaluated separately.',
'Wendy’s develops, operates and franchises quick-service restaurants. Its disclosed segments are Wendy’s U.S., Wendy’s International, and Global Real Estate & Development. The first two divide a similar restaurant/franchising activity geographically; the third includes property and development activities with a different economic model.',
'The business serves restaurant consumers and franchise operators, including franchisees that rent restaurant premises. Consumer demand and franchisee economics therefore matter through different channels. Reviewed disclosures do not establish a reliable age, income or lifestyle distribution for restaurant customers; franchise-applicant wealth requirements are not consumer demographics.',
'End markets include quick-service dining, restaurant franchising and restaurant-property support. Restaurant sales depend on consumer spending and local competition, while royalties and rents also depend on franchisee performance. These exposures are related but should not be treated as a single homogeneous customer market.',
'The system is predominantly franchised, with retained company-operated restaurants and property interests. At FY2025 year-end, 5,546 of 5,969 U.S. restaurants and 1,417 of 1,428 international restaurants were franchised. Unit percentages do not equal revenue or profit percentages, and a high franchise share does not make the consolidated company wholly asset-light.',
'Revenue includes company-operated restaurant sales, sales-linked franchise royalties, franchise/development fees, advertising-fund revenue and rental income. Advertising-fund revenue has associated expenditure and should not be valued as if it were a high-margin royalty stream. Equity income from TimWen must not be added again as segment revenue.',
'Wendy’s participates as brand owner and franchise-system manager, a restaurant operator, and a property lessor/sublessor. Food procurement and distribution also involve outside partners. This combination differs from a food manufacturer, a pure restaurant operator, or a standalone property REIT.',
'The company serves the U.S. and international markets, including Canada and the U.K. At June 28, 2026, the disclosed network comprised 5,724 U.S. and 1,456 international restaurants. These counts describe a specific reporting date and must not be compared with FY2025 counts as if both measured the same date.',
'Analyst classification: a large established restaurant chain. FY2025 disclosures report 7,397 system restaurants and approximately 14,900 company employees. The employee count principally concerns company operations and does not include the entire franchise-system workforce; the size label is an interpretation, not a vendor rating.',
'Wendy’s specializes in hamburger-led quick-service dining, supplemented by chicken, sides, breakfast and Frosty products. Menu breadth and product promises vary by geography. In particular, U.S. breakfast availability and fresh-beef statements should not be extended automatically to every international location.',
None,
'Food reaches consumers through company-operated and franchised restaurants, with dine-in, takeaway, drive-through and delivery channels. Delivery may be ordered through company digital channels or third-party platforms at participating locations. Menu, pricing and availability can differ by location and delivery provider.',
'Meals are prepared and delivered through physical restaurant service, takeaway, drive-through and delivery. Franchise support and property services are separate business-to-business relationships. Digital ordering supports the restaurant delivery model; it does not turn the company into a software-subscription provider.',
'The company has menu pricing, franchise royalties/fees and property rents, each with a different pricing basis. FY2025 filings describe a 4% royalty under most standard U.S. agreements; the undated FAQ states 4–6% of NET sales, while another franchise page states 4–6% of GROSS sales. The website denominator discrepancy remains unresolved and should not be collapsed into a single verified rate.',
'Royalties and rents provide ongoing revenue relationships, but royalties remain sensitive to restaurant sales and rents remain exposed to contractual performance. Franchise fees, advertising funds and company-operated sales require separate treatment. Ongoing revenue is not equivalent to fixed, guaranteed subscription revenue.',
'Capital intensity varies across the business: franchising generally requires less direct restaurant investment, while company-operated restaurants, information systems and owned/leased properties still require capital. Management also discusses technology and development expenditure. A system-wide franchise percentage alone is insufficient to classify consolidated capital intensity.',
'Restaurant operations rely on staffing and scheduling. FY2025 company employment was approximately 14,900, with roughly one-third full-time and two-thirds part-time. This is not the headcount of all franchisees, and it does not by itself establish a comparable system-wide labor-productivity measure.',
'Food safety, employment, franchising, data protection and information-security requirements affect operations. Supplier reviews and employee food-safety training support risk controls. Rules differ by jurisdiction; reviewed evidence supports regulatory exposure but not a single quantified risk score.',
'The company positions its brand around food quality and value. However, Q2 2026 management remarks acknowledge execution problems in food quality and value perception. Promotional positioning therefore should not be treated as independent proof of competitive superiority, and no verified market-share or brand-strength score is assigned.',
'Fresh beef, prepared food and branded products such as Frosty form part of Wendy’s differentiation proposition. Fresh-beef statements have geographic limitations. Management’s Q2 2026 discussion of deteriorating execution distinguishes a brand promise from consistent delivery of that promise; differentiation should not automatically be scored as a demonstrated advantage.',
None,
'The annual report describes moderately seasonal restaurant operations, with summer generally stronger than winter, and exposure to consumer discretionary spending. Seasonality and economic cyclicality are different concepts. One quarter of same-restaurant sales does not identify a stable long-run demand elasticity.',
'Wendy’s is an established restaurant brand whose first restaurant opened in 1969. Brand history, the incorporation of legal entities and later reorganizations are different events. The original restaurant opening date is used to describe operating maturity, rather than substituting an older predecessor-company incorporation date.',
'Point-of-sale, kitchen and restaurant systems, digital ordering, mobile applications, loyalty and customer-management capabilities support operations. Technology is infrastructure for a restaurant/franchise business. Management aspirations to increase digital purchasing frequency are plans, not evidence of an already measured customer visit rate.',
'Using FY2025 disclosed segment revenue, the U.S. segment represented approximately 82.00%, International 7.03%, and Global Real Estate & Development 10.97%. The property segment spans geographies, so the latter two shares cannot simply be labeled overseas revenue. These are consolidated segment-revenue shares, not system-sales or customer-location shares.',
'The system relies on procurement organizations, food processors, distributors and quality controls. Fresh-beef cold-chain requirements and supplier auditing add coordination needs. Annual-report supplier and distributor concentration disclosures have specific geography and period boundaries and should not be generalized to the entire international system.',
'Most standard U.S. franchise agreements described in FY2025 filings have an initial 20-year term with a conditional 10-year extension, with a 25-year initial-term option. International arrangements vary. Franchise terms, property-lease terms and the remaining duration of leases where the company is a tenant are not interchangeable.',
'The operating model depends on Wendy’s trademarks and service marks, together with related copyrights, domains and trade secrets. Reviewed disclosures support brand and operating-system intellectual property. They do not support classifying Wendy’s as a patent-driven technology business.',
'The company and franchisees depend on the Wendy’s brand, food quality and consumer perception. The annual report identifies reputation risk, while Q2 2026 management remarks discuss quality and value concerns. Brand dependence is supported; a high current brand-strength score is not established by that dependence.'
]
for r,en in zip(d['core_facets'],texts):r['Description English']=en;r['Description Chinese']=r['Value Text'];r['English Text Type']='Analyst synthesis of cited English sources; not a verbatim quotation.'
segment={
'Product Category':'Hamburger-led quick-service food, including chicken products, sides, beverages and breakfast where offered. The quarterly menu description supports product scope; it does not establish category-level revenue shares. Menus and breakfast availability vary by market.',
'Market Position':'The business operates in quick-service dining. U.S. value-menu announcements illustrate value positioning, while international positioning depends on local markets. Promotional claims are issuer statements, not independent market-position rankings.',
'Distribution Model':'The restaurant network is predominantly franchised, with retained company-operated locations. FY2025 U.S. counts were 5,546 franchised and 423 company-operated; international counts were 1,417 and 11, respectively. These are unit counts, not revenue shares.',
'Store Footprint':'Physical restaurants support dine-in, takeaway, drive-through and delivery where available. The presence of a channel in company materials does not establish coverage at every location. International formats and digital availability require market-specific qualification.',
'Brand Strength':'The Wendy’s name supports an established franchise and licensing system. This is evidence of a brand-based operating model, not an independent valuation or consumer-awareness measure. Q2 management remarks about food-quality execution qualify any inference of uniformly strong current brand performance.',
'Purchase Frequency':'Customer-level visits or purchases per week were not established in reviewed sources. Dayparts and delivery availability describe occasions or channels, while traffic growth measures aggregate change. Neither is a substitute for an observed repeat-purchase frequency.',
'Customer Demographics':'Reviewed sources do not establish a reliable segment-level customer age, income or lifestyle distribution. Franchise-applicant liquidity and net-worth requirements concern prospective business partners and must not be used as restaurant-consumer demographics.',
'Inventory Model':'Fresh-beef disclosures support a perishable, temperature-controlled supply-chain requirement in specified markets. This is a limited ingredient/geography observation. It does not establish all-ingredient inventory practices or a verified inventory-turnover metric.',
'Geographic Footprint':'FY2025 restaurant counts were 5,969 in the U.S. and 1,428 internationally; Q2 2026 counts were 5,724 and 1,456. International disclosures identify 38 countries/territories outside the U.S. Reporting-date changes are not contradictions, and undated website lower bounds do not replace dated counts.',
'Pricing Power':'No defensible segment-level price-elasticity rating is assigned. The call describes U.S. traffic falling 12.5% and average check rising 5.6%, with discounting, breakfast hours and product mix contributing. Average-check movement is not a clean measure of pure pricing power, and U.S. figures must not be transferred to international markets.',
'Franchise versus Company-operated Mix':'Calculated from FY2025 restaurant counts: U.S. franchised units were 5,546 / 5,969, or 92.91%; international units were 1,417 / 1,428, or 99.23%. The denominator is the relevant geographic restaurant segment. These percentages are not franchise-revenue or EBITDA weights.',
'Revenue Streams / Advertising Fund Treatment':'FY2025 U.S. revenue comprised company sales of $887.512m, royalties of $429.039m, franchise fees of $84.101m and advertising funds of $384.472m. International amounts were $28.813m, $75.508m, $11.027m and $37.613m. Advertising revenue has associated costs and should not be treated as a royalty-equivalent margin stream.',
'Franchise Royalty / Fee Terms':'FY2025 filings describe most standard U.S. agreements with a 4% royalty and $50,000 technical-assistance fee; Canadian standard arrangements use 4% and C$50,000. Other countries and agreements vary. Current undated website pages differ on NET versus GROSS sales as the royalty denominator; that discrepancy remains unresolved.',
'Franchise Contract Duration':'Most standard U.S. agreements described in the annual report run initially for 20 years, with a conditional 10-year extension and a 25-year initial option. Canadian standard terms are generally 20 plus a conditional 10 years; other international terms vary. These are contract terms, not weighted remaining durations.',
'Restaurant Formats / Channel Scope':'Traditional restaurants may offer dine-in, takeaway, drive-through and delivery; nontraditional locations and locally adapted designs also exist. Channel availability is location-dependent. U.S. delivery-page features should not be assumed to apply identically across all international markets.',
'Recent Operating Demand Signal':'Q2 2026 U.S. same-restaurant sales declined 7.0% and system sales declined 8.2%; international same-restaurant sales declined 2.3% while system sales rose 3.4%. These metrics have different denominators. They are dated operating observations, not forecasts or stand-alone measures of pricing power.',
'Property / Asset Type':'This segment concerns restaurant properties and franchise infrastructure, including owned sites leased to franchisees and third-party sites subleased to franchisees. Its asset exposure differs from general office or residential property. Restaurant operations and property interests should not be double-counted.',
'Ownership / Operating Role':'The segment combines property ownership and leasing, head-leasing and subleasing, joint-venture income and development support. The annual and quarterly filings establish this mixed role. A historical company blog also describes Build-to-Suit leasing/subleasing directly from Wendy’s; it does not verify current portfolio counts or independent property ownership.',
'Tenant / Customer Type':'The principal disclosed customer relationship is with Wendy’s franchise operators leasing or subleasing restaurant premises. Rental exposure is therefore tied to the franchise ecosystem rather than directly billed to diners. A quantitative tenant-concentration rating is not established by this qualitative relationship.',
'Revenue Composition':'FY2025 segment revenue included $235.750m of rent and $3.056m of franchise/development-related fees, totaling $238.806m. The existing LSEG segment-total snapshot agrees with the annual-report total. TimWen equity income is not an additional revenue component to add to this table.',
'Geographic Exposure':'The segment is described as global and includes the Canadian TimWen property venture. Reviewed disclosures do not provide a complete usable country-by-country property exposure breakdown for this segment. Consolidated geography tables and the International restaurant segment are not substitutes.',
'Lease Economics / Pass-through':'Filings describe long-term leases and subleases, including contract-dependent escalation, renewal, sales-related rent and cost pass-through arrangements. These features vary by agreement. The evidence does not support labeling every lease fully triple-net or assigning an invented portfolio capitalization rate.',
'Portfolio Size / Owned versus Leased':'At FY2025 year-end, disclosed franchisee-operated property interests included 491 owned properties leased out and 1,146 leased properties subleased. This is a dated property-interest count. It should not be added to the total restaurant count, which includes other property arrangements.',
'Remaining Tenant Lease Term / WALE':'A usable weighted average remaining term for leases to franchisee tenants was not established. Group lessee disclosures, including finance-lease and operating-lease remaining terms, measure Wendy’s obligations as tenant. Those measures cannot populate this lessor-side facet.',
'Joint Venture Structure':'The segment includes the company’s share of income from the Canadian TimWen restaurant-property joint venture. Both annual and quarterly segment descriptions identify this exposure. It is part of the reported property/development segment, not a fourth reportable business segment.',
'Development / Advisory Services':'Disclosed activities include franchise-transfer coordination and development-related services. Official franchise pages describe site selection, design, construction and related support. A service being advertised does not prove every service has separately disclosed revenue in this segment; historical Build-to-Suit statements are not current portfolio counts.'}
for r in d['facets']:r['Description English']=segment[r['Facet']];r['Description Chinese']=(r['Value Text'] or '未找到足够证据；保留未知。')+'\n\n'+r['Evidence Summary']+'\n\n'+r.get('Limitations','');r['English Text Type']='Analyst synthesis, not verbatim source text.'
p.write_text(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
h=Path('outputs/company_research_viewer/index.html');t=h.read_text();import re
t=re.sub(r'const wendyPilot=.*?;\n',lambda m:'const wendyPilot='+json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)+';\n',t,count=1)
t=t.replace('<header><h1>','<header><select id="languageSwitch" aria-label="Language / 语言" style="float:right"><option value="en">English</option><option value="zh">中文</option></select><h1>',1)
t+='''
<script>
let displayLanguage=localStorage.getItem('researchLanguage')||'en';
const uiPairs=[['公司研究 · 当前结果','Company Research · Current Results'],['按公司查看当前候选、已填写的 Facet 和引用来源。行业专属评分与分部加权尚未完成。','Browse company facets, segment profiles and evidence. Industry scoring and segment weighting remain incomplete.'],['公司检索','Find a company'],['560 个目标公司','560 target companies'],['上市候选公司','Public candidates'],['全部角色','All roles'],['当前候选','Comparable candidates'],['公司 Facet','Company facets'],['行业专属 Facet','Industry facets'],['业务分部','Business segments'],['引用来源','Evidence sources'],['财务与数据内容','Financial datasets'],['完成范围：','Coverage:'],['Wendy’s 已补充逐分部行业 Facet 试点；其他公司尚未批量填表。当前可比评分尚未纳入这些新字段，也未进行分部加权，不能作为完整方法的最终结论。Target 仅官网用于选择评分；缺失信息不假定为零。','Wendy’s is the pilot. Other companies have not received this enrichment. Existing comparable scores exclude these new fields and segment weighting. Missing evidence is not assumed to be zero.']];
function translateShell(){document.documentElement.lang=displayLanguage==='en'?'en':'zh';document.title=displayLanguage==='en'?'Company Research · Current Results':'公司研究 · 当前结果';const walker=document.createTreeWalker(document.body,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);let n;while(n=walker.nextNode()){if(['SCRIPT','STYLE'].includes(n.parentElement.tagName)||n.parentElement.closest('#content'))continue;for(const [zh,en] of uiPairs){if(n.nodeValue.trim()===(displayLanguage==='en'?zh:en))n.nodeValue=n.nodeValue.replace(displayLanguage==='en'?zh:en,displayLanguage==='en'?en:zh)}}}
function bilingualCard(r){const en=displayLanguage==='en';return `<article class="card"><h3>${esc(en?r.Facet:(labels[r.Facet]||r.Facet))}</h3>${r['Segment Name']?`<p class="small">${esc(r['Segment Name'])} · ${esc(r.Industry)}</p>`:''}<span class="badge">${r['Value Text']==null?(en?'Evidence gap':'证据不足'):(en?'Source-supported research / interpretation':'有来源的研究整理 / 分析')}</span><div class="value">${esc(en?(r['Description English']||'Not established in reviewed sources.'):(r['Description Chinese']||r['Value Text']))}</div><p class="small">${en?'English descriptions are research summaries, not verbatim source quotations.':'中英文均为来源整理摘要，不是逐字原文。'}</p><details><summary>${en?'Documents, reporting periods and links':'文件、报告期及来源链接'}</summary>${(r['Source Claims']||[]).map(s=>`<p><strong>${esc(s.source_id)} · ${esc(s.document_type)}</strong><br>${en?'Filed / published':'提交 / 发布'}: ${esc(s.publication_or_filing_date)}<br>${en?'Fact period':'事实期'}: ${esc(s.fact_period)}<br>${links(s.url)}<br>${esc(s.review_scope)}</p>`).join('')}</details><p class="small">${en?'Issuer filings, the corporate website and management calls share an issuer origin. Multiple documents are not necessarily independent corroboration. Historical or undated material does not establish current facts.':'年报、官网和管理层电话会同属发行人来源；多份文件不等于独立验证。历史或无日期材料不能自动证明当前事实。'}</p></article>`}
showWendyCore=function(){const en=displayLanguage==='en';$('content').innerHTML=`<h2>${en?'Wendy’s · Company facets · 28 / 30 populated':'Wendy’s · 公司通用 Facet · 28 / 30 已填'}</h2><p class="notice">${en?'Expanded-source research profile. Existing website-only target selection scores have not been recalculated. Annual-report facts retain their FY2025 dates; no IPO registration filing was relied upon.':'扩展来源研究档案。现有官网限定评分未重算；年报事实保留 FY2025 日期，本次未依赖 IPO 文件。'}</p>`+wendyPilot.core_facets.map(bilingualCard).join('')};
showWendyIndustry=function(){const en=displayLanguage==='en';$('content').innerHTML=`<h2>${en?'Wendy’s · Segment-specific industry facets':'Wendy’s · 逐分部行业 Facet'}</h2><p>${en?'42 fields across three reportable segments. U.S. and International share a restaurant/franchising industry; property and development activities are evaluated separately. Descriptions distinguish business scope, dated observations and evidence limitations.':'三个披露分部、42 项字段。美国和国际同属餐饮加盟行业，物业开发业务另行分析。描述分别说明业务范围、事实日期及证据局限。'}</p><select id="pilotSegment"><option value="ALL">${en?'All segments':'全部分部'}</option>${wendyPilot.segments.map(s=>`<option value="${s.id}">${esc(s.name)}</option>`).join('')}</select><div id="segmentCards"></div>`;const draw=()=>{$('segmentCards').innerHTML=wendyPilot.facets.filter(r=>pilotSegment==='ALL'||r['Segment ID']===pilotSegment).map(bilingualCard).join('')};$('pilotSegment').value=pilotSegment;$('pilotSegment').onchange=e=>{pilotSegment=e.target.value;draw()};draw()};
const previousSources=showWendySources;
showWendySources=function(){if(displayLanguage==='zh')return previousSources();$('content').innerHTML='<h2>Wendy’s · 14 evidence sources</h2><p>Search is a discovery channel; citations link to the underlying documents. Two transcript hosts reproduce the same call and are not independent corporate evidence.</p>'+wendyPilot.sources.map(s=>`<article class="card"><h3>${esc(s.name)}</h3>${links(s.url)}<p>Filed / published: ${esc(s.date)}<br>Fact period: ${esc(s.period)}<br>Section: ${esc(s.section)}</p><p>${esc(s.origin||'Issuer / provider source; independence not established.')}</p></article>`).join('')};
const originalRender=render;render=function(){originalRender();translateShell()};
$('languageSwitch').value=displayLanguage;$('languageSwitch').onchange=e=>{displayLanguage=e.target.value;localStorage.setItem('researchLanguage',displayLanguage);render()};translateShell();if(current)render();
</script>
'''
